<pre>
<code>
---
platform: linux

inputs:
- name: platform-automation-tasks
  # Concourse input: packaged Platform Automation tasks (task script and windows-automation/)
- name: windows-iso
  optional: true
  # Optional. Provide when using ISO upload mode (ISO on the task container / Concourse resource).
  # Not required when ISO_PATH points at an ISO already on a vSphere datastore, or in template mode.

outputs:
- name: logs
  # Build and step logs copied from the automation working directory.
- name: stemcell
  # BOSH Windows stemcell tarball: bosh-stemcell-*-vsphere-esxi-windows*-go_agent.tgz

params:
  DEBUG_MODE: "false"
  # Optional. Set to "true" to enable shell trace (set -x) in build scripts.

  # --- vCenter (required) ---
  VCENTER_SERVER: ""
  VCENTER_USERNAME: ""
  VCENTER_PASSWORD: ""
  VCENTER_INSECURE_CONNECTION: "true"
  VCENTER_DATACENTER: ""
  VCENTER_DATASTORE: ""
  VCENTER_NETWORK: ""
  # Use cluster or host as appropriate for your environment:
  VCENTER_CLUSTER: ""
  VCENTER_HOST: ""
  # Optional:
  # VCENTER_FOLDER: ""
  # VCENTER_RESOURCE_POOL: ""

  # --- Build mode (set one source; see Task inputs and outputs) ---
  # ISO already on datastore (vCenter path):
  # ISO_PATH: '[datastore-name]/path/to/windows.iso'
  # ISO from task / windows-iso input (path relative to workspace or absolute in container):
  # ISO_PATH_LOCAL: "windows-iso/*.iso"
  # Template mode (no Packer install from ISO):
  # TEMPLATE_PATH: '/Datacenter/vm/Templates/my-windows-template'
  # Optional: existing VM mode (clone this VM; no Packer ISO install). Use instead of ISO or template when applicable.
  # EXISTING_BASE_VM_NAME: ""

  # --- Windows & stemcell (required) ---
  WINDOWS_USERNAME: "Administrator"
  WINDOWS_PASSWORD: ""
  PATCH_VERSION: ""
  # e.g. 2019.12.3 or a numeric patch segment required by stembuild
  WINDOWS_VERSION: "2019"
  # 2019 | 2022 | 2025 — must match stembuild binary and templates

  # --- Network (required) ---
  STATIC_IP: ""
  SUBNET_MASK: ""
  GATEWAY: ""
  DNS_SERVERS: "8.8.8.8,8.8.4.4"
  # Comma-separated list; converted to HCL list in generated vars

  # --- Optional ---
  # KEEP_BASE_VM: "false"
  # ISO mode only: keep the Packer-created base VM after cloning to target (string "true" / "false")
  # TEMPLATE_NAME: ""
  # ISO mode: optional final template name after successful build
  # PRODUCT_KEY: ""
  # HTTP_PROXY: ""
  # HTTPS_PROXY: ""
  # NO_PROXY: ""
  # ENABLE_WINDOWS_UPDATES: "true"
  # LOG_LEVEL: "INFO"
  # JUMPER_HOST: ""
  # JUMPER_USER: ""
  # JUMPER_PASSWORD: ""

run:
  path: platform-automation-tasks/tasks/build-windows-stemcell.sh

</code>
</pre>

<p class="note">
The Concourse input name for the tasks volume is arbitrary. If you name it something other than <code>platform-automation-tasks</code>, set <code>file:</code> and <code>run.path</code> so they are prefixed with your input name (for example <code>my-tasks/tasks/build-windows-stemcell.sh</code>). The paths under that input must match the Platform Automation tasks layout.
</p>
